            0.889,
            0.117
          ],
          "content": [
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": "Without a rigid cell wall, animal cells can change shape easily. This cellular flexibility supports the overall movement and functioning of animal tissues."
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "index": 1,
          "bbox": [
            0.223,
            0.119,
            0.89,
            0.204
          ],
          "content": [
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": "The plant cell wall is primarily made of cellulose, a type of carbohydrate formed by many glucose units linked together. Cellulose in our diet acts as roughage, helping in digestion. Some microorganisms, like fungi and bacteria also have a cell wall to provide protection and structural support to their cells."
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "paragraph_title",
          "index": 2,
          "bbox": [
            0.237,
            0.209,
            0.492,
            0.235
          ],
          "content": [
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": "Pause and Ponder"
            }
          ],
          "level": 2
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "index": 3,
          "bbox": [
            0.255,
            0.238,
            0.866,
            0.286
          ],
          "content": [
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": "1. What argument would you give for the necessity of a cell wall in plants usually fixed in one place versus in animals usually moving from one place to the other?"
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "index": 4,
          "bbox": [
            0.256,
            0.287,
            0.865,
            0.32
          ],
          "content": [
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": "2. What consequences would you predict for a plant cell if its cell wall were to become as flexible as a cell membrane?"
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "index": 5,
          "bbox": [
            0.256,
            0.322,
            0.865,
            0.356
          ],
          "content": [
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": "3. Why is it important to cut the two potato pieces in roughly equal size and measure their initial weight before placing them in different liquids?"
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "paragraph_title",
          "index": 6,
          "bbox": [
            0.224,
            0.382,
            0.884,
            0.404
          ],
          "content": [
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": "2.3 The Cell Interior — A Coordinated Working System"
